From a51df7c9475fbb699f55cfe2dcac08f6e172a9c4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Maxime=20M=C3=A9r=C3=A9?= <maxime.mere@foss.st.com>
Date: Fri, 10 Jul 2026 17:32:02 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] hwrng: stm32 - return actual error code from clk_bulk_get_all
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Return the error code from devm_clk_bulk_get_all() instead of masking
it with -EINVAL. This is critical for supporting EPROBE_DEFER when
clock dependencies are not yet available, allowing the probe to be
retried rather than failing permanently.

Change-Id: I21324e4cecfe9e0b6c99d8adaef6953abbbaec49
Signed-off-by: Maxime Méré <maxime.mere@foss.st.com>
Reviewed-on: https://gerrit.st.com/c/mpu/oe/st/linux-stm32/+/587565
Reviewed-by: Yann GAUTIER <yann.gautier@foss.st.com>
ACI: CIBUILD <MDG-smet-aci-builds@list.st.com>
Domain-Review: Yann GAUTIER <yann.gautier@foss.st.com>
---
 drivers/char/hw_random/stm32-rng.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/char/hw_random/stm32-rng.c b/drivers/char/hw_random/stm32-rng.c
index b1e8531cb40a..0006cd8617ca 100644
--- a/drivers/char/hw_random/stm32-rng.c
+++ b/drivers/char/hw_random/stm32-rng.c
@@ -610,7 +610,7 @@ static int stm32_rng_probe(struct platform_device *ofdev)
 
 	ret = devm_clk_bulk_get_all(dev, &priv->clk_bulk);
 	if (ret != priv->data->nb_clock)
-		return dev_err_probe(dev, -EINVAL, "Failed to get clocks: %d\n", ret);
+		return dev_err_probe(dev, ret, "Failed to get clocks: %d\n", ret);
 
 	if (priv->data->nb_clock == 2) {
 		const char *id = priv->clk_bulk[1].id;
-- 
2.53.0

